cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite both the dataset and the paper."
title: "CRUSTPairs: A Cross-Language Dataset of Paired C and Rust Solutions"
type: dataset
version: 1.0.0
# The day the Zenodo record was published. The DOI below is the version DOI
# and resolves to exactly these files; the concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23888784
# resolves to whatever version is newest.
date-released: 2026-11-02
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23888785
repository-code: "https://github.com/hejlevoj/crosslang-c-rust-similarity"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23888785"

# Order follows the paper. The ORCIDs are the ones on the published Zenodo
# record; Hejlek's is still missing there and here.
authors:
  - family-names: "Hejlek"
    given-names: "Vojtěch"
    affiliation: "Faculty of Information Technology in Prague"
    # orcid: not yet supplied
  - family-names: "Almeida"
    given-names: "Leonardo Jesus"
    affiliation: "University of São Paulo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-1543-1631"
  - family-names: "Lopes"
    given-names: "Alneu de Andrade"
    affiliation: "University of São Paulo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3112-4746"

abstract: >-
  1857 pairs of C and Rust implementations of the same competitive programming
  problem, drawn from IBM Project CodeNet and xCodeEval, normalised,
  deduplicated, and stratified into difficulty tiers by zero-shot
  cross-language embedding similarity. Each record carries its problem
  statement, provenance, SPDX licence expression, difficulty tier and raw
  similarity score, and a frozen stratified train/validation/test split.

keywords:
  - cross-language code similarity
  - code retrieval
  - C
  - Rust
  - program translation
  - memory safety
  - dataset

# The licence above is the one that governs the aggregate, because 1018 of the
# 1857 pairs derive from xCodeEval under CC BY-NC 4.0. The 839 CodeNet-derived
# pairs are CDLA-Permissive-2.0 and the accompanying code is MIT; every record
# carries its own SPDX expression in the `license` field. See DATA_LICENSES.md.
